# G-ACE SERVER_AI BOOTSTRAP

PROFILE=SERVER_AI

1. Read `/home/admin1/server-core/README.md`.
2. Read `/home/admin1/server-core/docs/LOAD_SCOPE.md`.
3. Read `/home/admin1/server-core/operations/github-project-rule-plane.json`.
4. Resolve canonical SERVER_AI rule item #16 and GitHub Project #1 Current when GitHub access is available.
5. Load only the target repository Current and the minimum authority/source/test required for the task.

Do not default-load GPT_CHAT rule item #17.
Do not load all server-core documents.
Do not load unrelated repositories or historical Notion material by default.

Execution invariants:
- Fresh Current before mutation.
- Reuse existing verified evidence/code/tool before new implementation.
- Prefer sufficient deterministic checks and useful AVAILABLE_VERIFIED tools; do not require another AI/service for ordinary work.
- Keep FACT / INFERENCE / UNKNOWN separate.
- Keep SOURCE / TEST / CI / MERGE / DEPLOY / RUNTIME separate.
- Never expose Secret/Token values.
- Production-resident services use Docker / Docker Compose.
- Respect Master approval boundaries.
- Commit/PR is the GitHub work report when files change.

If Project/rule Current cannot be read, do not guess. Use the local server-core bootstrap only for safe routing and mark `RULE_PLANE_CURRENT=NOT_VERIFIED`.

server-core is the Workspace control room. Project implementation remains in the owning repository.

Master selects the lead AI. The lead may use already configured in-client subagents when useful, preserving their roles and existing model/cost settings; do not force a chain or replace the lead. External AI/service launches remain Master's choice.
Use normal local editing/shell/testing tools. GPT app CHAT ServerTerminal/Actions, Notion, per-turn loop and output conventions do not apply. Create necessary focused tests and finish the assigned work; do not stop merely because an existing test is absent.
Report material progress and evidence concisely in Japanese. No mandatory model-name prefix, internal-thinking language, full-log output or per-file narrative. Keep secrets private and respect real installed permissions.
